      "id": "TDE-01",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-torsion-product",
      "title": "The torsion product attains coefficient norm one",
      "statement": "For the good elliptic model at p≥5 the multiplication series satisfies e²=T²UG. Here U is integral of constant term 1, and G=p²∏(A−x_PT²) runs over the p²−1 nonzero complex p-torsion classes with transported x-coordinates. The largest coefficient norm of G is |p²|∏max(1,|x_P|)=1.",
      "hypotheses": "The model has p-adically integral invariants, unit discriminant and the compatible homothetic complex lattice. The p-adic absolute value is used after transport by the given field isomorphism. No CM or inertness is needed for this identity.",
